1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,294
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:05,046
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,760
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:15,724
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,184
[Karla] <i>What are you doing</i>
<i>here at the shop?</i>

7
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:20,061
[Uno] I came to have a suit made.

8
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:24,399
They told me this is really
the best place. Good tailoring.

9
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:25,775
[Gavin on the phone, in English]
<i>Did you kill Grandpa?</i>

10
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,318
We'll talk about it when you get home.

11
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:29,487
Our deal was that today,
you'll give us back the kid.

12
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:32,532
The child already believes I'm her mother.

13
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,325
Can we just make it real?

14
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,368
[in English] Of course not.

15
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:38,079
Audrey escaped,
and the child is the only way

16
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,623
to bring Audrey back here,
so she won't speak.

17
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,292
[Martina] Just think what Atoy will do

18
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:45,545
when he finds out Ibyang
is really his child.

19
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:46,838
PREVIOUSLY

20
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:48,423
Ibyang is Atoy's child?

21
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:49,799
[in English] That's none of your business.

22
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,676
I'll tell Atoy everything.

23
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,219
- Ouch, ouch!
- [in English] Not so fast!

24
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,263
[grunts and groans]

25
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:58,141
- [Karla] <i>We don't even know him.</i>
- [keypad beeping]

26
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:00,560
<i>He just suddenly appeared here.</i>

27
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:03,396
[Charmi] <i>You know Ibyang's real parent?!</i>

28
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,106
- It's Atoy.
- [in English] For real?!

29
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,192
[Paldo] <i>Isn't his mission finished yet?</i>

30
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:10,612
This is the longest time

31
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:13,323
he hasn't sent word while on a mission.

32
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,365
I don't know the access code.

33
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,202
[Uno] <i>Do you know the combinations?</i>

34
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:20,163
[in English] Do you know this woman?

35
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:23,708
[in English] Don't tell me
that you don't know them.

36
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:26,211
Don't drag them into this.

37
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:28,296
[in English] But I will
make her scream in pain.

38
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,672
[grunts]

39
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:35,220
[gasps]

40
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:36,763
[music fades]

41
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:42,685
Oh, miss, I'll go to the shop first.
I'll lend Paldo some clothes.

42
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:45,063
I'll check there.
Maybe some things survived the fire.

43
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,732
You can borrow Atoy's T-Shirt
from his room.

44
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:48,983
Ah, can I?

45
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,360
Maybe even borrow his briefs.

46
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:51,444
- Oh.
- Atoy's.

47
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:52,445
You're ridiculous.

48
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:54,280
Looks like it, huh. [chuckles]

49
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:56,783
Mom! Brother Emerson! Is Uno inside?

50
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,493
He is. Why?

51
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:00,453
You shouldn't have let him in.

52
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,412
- Why?
- Huh?

53
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:02,872
I think he's a spy.

54
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,083
Maybe he works for Red Regalia.

55
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,210
- What?! Are you sure?
- Huh?

56
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,629
[suspicious music playing]

57
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,884
- [device blips]
- Caught you!

58
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,469
[Karla] I knew it. My suspicion was right!

59
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:17,512
[growls]

60
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,681
[grunts and groans]

61
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,892
[Karla shouts]

62
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:23,810
[Uno] I know Atoy!

63
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:26,729
- [Karla] You think you can escape!
- [Uno] Mercado sent me!

64
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:28,982
[suave theme music playing]

65
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,591
[music fades]

66
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:56,467
Sorry, everyone.

67
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:59,178
I didn't introduce myself right away.

68
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:00,889
[Cita inhales]

69
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:05,435
The truth is that
I didn't want anyone else to know.

70
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:09,981
Because national security is at stake.

71
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:14,944
Actually, I work for Colonel Mercado.

72
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,863
[pensive music playing]

73
00:03:16,946 --> 00:03:19,198
[Emerson] Ahh.

74
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:20,658
Is that so?

75
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:26,039
Oh, so that's why your moves
are similar to Atoy's moves and mine.

76
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:30,376
Right? So cool. Like Chuck Norris action.

77
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,294
[chuckles]

78
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:34,756
So, you're a tracker too,
like Brother Atoy?

79
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:41,679
That's right, and Sir Padua
is our primary, and he's the best.

80
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,640
[Emerson] Hmm.

81
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:49,646
You know, actually,
I really want to be a tracker too.

82
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,356
- [Uno] Really?
- Yes. I think I can.

83
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:55,485
Because I've been with Atoy,
so I know what to do.

84
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,696
Where do you apply for an interview?
Where do you submit a biodata?

85
00:03:58,780 --> 00:03:59,614
I want to apply.

86
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,532
Because I have medical clearance.
It's complete.

87
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:02,450
- I have SSS too.
- Emerson!

88
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:04,077
- Emerson, stop.
- And I also have…

89
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:04,994
I also have, ah…

90
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:08,206
Later. Ask questions later
about changing your career.

91
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:10,291
- But if I have complete…
- Enough for now.

92
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:13,795
The important question now is,
why are you here?

93
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:20,009
I need to secure the laptop
that was turned over to Sir Padua.

94
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,929
[in English] Laptop, laptop.

95
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:25,139
- Wait.
- [suspicious music playing]

96
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:27,892
[Atoy] <i>This is the device I extracted</i>
<i>from the Zahran Embassy, sir.</i>

97
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,018
Why is it here again?

98
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:31,562
[Mercado on the tablet] <i>I'll send you</i>
<i>the details of your mission.</i>

99
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:35,483
[in English] <i>But this laptop</i>
<i>is for your safekeeping.</i>

100
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:38,361
That's the one… That's…

101
00:04:38,444 --> 00:04:41,990
That's the one your boss sent here?

102
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:44,325
- The one in the…
- [Uno] Oh, oh…

103
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:45,952
hard case, like for a gun?

104
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,829
- [Uno, in English] Yes, exactly.
- The heavy one? That one?

105
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:51,833
[Emerson] I was here then!
I was with Atoy when it was sent here.

106
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:54,460
- I saw it.
- So, where is it hidden?

107
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:56,796
I didn't see.
I don't know where Atoy put it.

108
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:58,840
Of course, he was the one who hid it.

109
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:00,508
- [sneaky music playing]
- [Cita stammers]

110
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:01,801
You're so confusing to talk to.

111
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,177
Wait, wait.

112
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:08,474
If you really work with Atoy,
why don't you just ask him?

113
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:09,851
Where is he?

114
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:11,644
[in English] He's compromised.

115
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:12,729
What?!

116
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:13,938
[pensive music playing]

117
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:19,110
We tried calling him,
and we went to his last location.

118
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:20,987
But he's really missing in action.

119
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:25,867
And we suspect he was captured.

120
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,161
What do you mean?!

121
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:29,912
Something happened to him?!

122
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,122
What? Is Atoy okay?!

123
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,623
- Is he alive?!
- Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom.

124
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,459
- Miss, miss.
- Don't say that.

125
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:35,918
- [Emerson] Miss. Sit down first, miss.
- [gasps]

126
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,420
- No.
- Sit down first, miss.

127
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:39,380
- He's okay…
- [pensive music playing]

128
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:43,926
I'm very sorry, but we really don't know.

129
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:46,637
But I'm being honest with you.

130
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:50,391
- [Cita whimpers]
- Everything you fear could happen.

131
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,435
My God. [sobs]

132
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,982
[Cita] So-- How--

133
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:00,443
Who can we ask?

134
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:04,197
Where can we go to find him?
What… What can we do?

135
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,865
[tense music playing]

136
00:06:05,948 --> 00:06:08,034
[Cita] Oh my God.

137
00:06:18,669 --> 00:06:20,088
[Red] Zip it up.

138
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:24,675
[mysterious music playing]

139
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:40,441
[ominous music playing]

140
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:45,530
[ambulance siren wailing]

141
00:06:47,448 --> 00:06:49,784
I hope you catch those thieves.

142
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:52,578
I never thought it would come to this.

143
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:55,414
I lost my father because of them.

144
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,707
Don't worry, sir.

145
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,543
We'll do everything we can.

146
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:02,505
And if you can follow us to the station,
to give your official statement.

147
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,424
[in English] I'll be there with my lawyer.

148
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,510
All right, sir. Our condolences.

149
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,438
[sighs]

150
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,607
[line ringing]

151
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,317
[phone ringing]

152
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:26,237
[suspicious music playing]

153
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:28,865
[in English] Yes?

154
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,032
[Red on the phone] <i>Where are you?</i>

155
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,868
Do you have Ibyang with you?

156
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:34,120
[in English] No, not yet.

157
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,663
Olga ran away from me.

158
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:39,625
[in English] But don't worry.
Our men are searching for her as we speak.

159
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,712
This night has way too many screw-ups.

160
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,964
[in English] We need that kid.

161
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:46,924
Come back here.

162
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:49,385
[tense music playing]

163
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:00,229
[music fades]

164
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,861
Lord.

165
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:08,613
[sobs]

166
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:12,783
I know You see everything.

167
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:15,536
[sobs]

168
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:20,500
I believe You have not abandoned Atoy.

169
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:25,004
[melodramatic music playing]

170
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,757
Who's that?

171
00:08:30,259 --> 00:08:31,969
The one on your necklace.

172
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,768
Saint Anthony of Padua.

173
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:44,440
Patron of lost people.

174
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:49,111
[Lily] Have you prayed to him?

175
00:08:51,572 --> 00:08:57,995
If that saint helps find the lost,

176
00:08:58,496 --> 00:08:59,997
maybe it can be reversed?

177
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:04,293
Maybe he can help

178
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,713
stop Samir from finding
your child and her mother.

179
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,018
[Atoy] <i>Please, Saint Anthony.</i>

180
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,730
<i>Please provide safety</i>
<i>for Audrey and Janine.</i>

181
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:28,192
<i>And also, the people</i>
<i>who are important to me.</i>

182
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:31,404
[Cita] And if he's in danger…

183
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:33,114
[sobs]

184
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:35,950
Save him, Lord.

185
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,496
[Atoy] <i>Give me strength too</i>

186
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,082
<i>to overcome this trial.</i>

187
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:47,044
[sobs]

188
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,630
I pray he comes home.

189
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:52,883
[sobbing]

190
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,726
[Atoy] <i>So I can still be</i>
<i>with my family, Saint Anthony,</i>

191
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:04,186
<i>and the people important to me.</i>

192
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:26,792
[winces] Ouch.

193
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:28,586
So dramatic.

194
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:30,421
In a fight, you're not afraid to get hurt.

195
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:33,424
Just a little alcohol and you act like…

196
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,259
It stings!

197
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,346
Of course, it's the face.
It stings, right?

198
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,973
So, your toughness is fake?

199
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,477
And your cuteness is fake too.

200
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,603
[Uno] Mmm-hmm.

201
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,355
Because the truth is,

202
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:49,982
you just want to get inside
Brother Atoy's house.

203
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,734
[light music playing]

204
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:55,529
Sorry, but you can't fool me.

205
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:58,157
[clicks tongue, sighs]

206
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,325
Sorry.

207
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:02,411
That's really my mission.

208
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:06,916
To get inside
and take the laptop, that's all.

209
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:13,381
I understand.
That's also Brother Atoy's job.

210
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:15,758
To pretend for the mission.

211
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:20,137
Honestly, I really admire Brother Atoy.

212
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:25,017
So, you admire me too?

213
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:29,605
Ouch, ouch! What's wrong? You…

214
00:11:30,189 --> 00:11:31,607
Are you angry?

215
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:34,193
Or you just can't admit the truth?

216
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:35,611
[pensive music playing]

217
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,488
You know, Karla,

218
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:40,032
when I first saw you,

219
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:43,369
I really found you beautiful.

220
00:11:43,452 --> 00:11:45,913
Yes. That's not fake.

221
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,417
How about you?

222
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:54,171
Can you admit to me that you like me too?

223
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:58,676
I won't admit anything to you
because I don't like you.

224
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:01,887
Really?

225
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,307
Why? Are you taken?

226
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:09,728
Or maybe… Maybe you already
like someone else?

227
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:13,149
[Uno] Hmm?

228
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,733
[in English] Yes.

229
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:17,820
[in English] Silence means yes, Karla.

230
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:19,321
[music fades]

231
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,073
But you're not sure.

232
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:27,455
Because I think
I'm better than the one you like.

233
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,335
Since you didn't answer me right away.

234
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:37,423
[pensive music playing]

235
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:38,966
Whatever.

236
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:42,136
Think whatever you want.

237
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,056
[in English] Okay.

238
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,402
If Atoy is missing…

239
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:03,824
…I'm sure he'll be found.
Let's trust Saint Anthony of Padua.

240
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:05,576
- Yes, Father.
- [Nestor] Yes.

241
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:06,702
[Nestor] Father is right.

242
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:09,497
Atoy even shares
the same name as our saint.

243
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,457
I'm sure he won't be abandoned.

244
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:15,920
To be sure, we'll hold a vigil for him.
Right, Father?

245
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:16,879
Yes, and…

246
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:22,384
I'll also help find a sponsor,
so that even if the vigil lasts all night,

247
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:25,095
the people of Tabang Lupa won't go hungry.

248
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:26,639
There. Count me in.

249
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:29,016
[in English] Free pares mami
for the first vigil.

250
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:30,309
I'll help you, Uncle.

251
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:32,811
Thank you so much, everyone.

252
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:37,274
But I think Brother Atoy
just went on vacation.

253
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:40,736
Of course, maybe he was sad
after losing Ibyang.

254
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:42,905
Where could he have gone?

255
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:44,907
Why, miss? Are you going with him?

256
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,116
Oh my.

257
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,576
- I was just asking.
- [horn honks in the distance]

258
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,119
Who's arriving?

259
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,246
Who's that?

260
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:54,124
[tires screech]

261
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,086
- It's Audrey.
- [door clicks shut]

262
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:58,587
[Ame and Cita] Audrey!

263
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,799
Audrey, it's late.
What are you doing here?

264
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:03,217
Why do you look like that?

265
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,218
You don't have pants.

266
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:08,180
[stammers] Oh, uh-- So-- Sorry.

267
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,557
Um, um…

268
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,350
[in English] It's a long story, but…

269
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:13,394
We're okay for now. Um…

270
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:15,354
Is Atoy here?

271
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:17,273
- [tense music playing]
- [muttering]

272
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:19,775
We're looking for him. We need his help.

273
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:21,277
Oh, no, Atoy isn't here.

274
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,320
We don't know where he is.

275
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,947
Atoy is missing.

276
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:28,284
[music swells]

277
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,625
You've been through a lot, Audrey.

278
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:39,753
You two should pray, okay.

279
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:42,756
[somber music playing]

280
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:45,175
You should rest now too.

281
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:47,553
Poor Janine.

282
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:50,139
So young, yet she's gone through so much.

283
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:53,517
[pensive music playing]

284
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:56,020
Thank you again.

285
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,272
Sorry for the trouble.

286
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:00,816
No, no. Don't worry about that.

287
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,818
Go upstairs now.

288
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,945
Stay in your old room, Janine.

289
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:07,406
[Audrey] Janine.

290
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:09,700
Come on.

291
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:12,995
Get some rest.

292
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:14,663
Thank you.

293
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:25,633
[phone ringing]

294
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:26,550
[in English] Mom?

295
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,427
[in English] Gavin, please.

296
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:31,055
[in English] Come home. For me?

297
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:34,350
Everything your father does
is to keep the family together.

298
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:37,102
No. I won't come home.

299
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,520
And don't look for me.

300
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,066
[in English] Gavin, please.

301
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:43,400
[in English] I don't want to lose you.

302
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:46,236
[in English] Please, come home. Please?

303
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:48,155
[in English] No!

304
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:49,657
[in English] He's evil!

305
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,741
[suspicious music playing]

306
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:53,494
[Gavin, in English] <i>Don't make me accept</i>
<i>that evil is normal!</i>

307
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:57,456
Mom, I don't care if you both cut me off.

308
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:58,916
[in English] Okay?

309
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:03,003
[in English] I don't want to be a Regalia.

310
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:06,173
And I'm ashamed to be the child
of your husband!

311
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,801
[Gavin on the phone] <i>Mom, I love you.</i>

312
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:13,180
But you're also enabling
Dad's evil behavior.

313
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:18,060
[in English] I can't be part
of something like that. I'm sorry.

314
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:21,313
[in English] I'm sorry, Mom, but…

315
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:23,816
Let's forget each other.

316
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,528
[Gavin sobs]

317
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,167
[sharp inhale]

318
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,293
[music fades]

319
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:47,089
[in English] S-Sorry.

320
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:50,634
Gavin, come in.

321
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:52,469
Sit down.

322
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:56,098
Sorry again.

323
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,435
[pensive music playing]

324
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:01,645
You don't need to apologize.

325
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:07,860
Honestly, I should apologize to you.

326
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,280
Because I thought
you were like your father.

327
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,243
But now I realize you're different.

328
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:18,454
You're good.

329
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:22,750
Because you even took Audrey
and Janine away from them.

330
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,044
Thank you.

331
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:28,547
It's okay.

332
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:33,343
I still carry our surname, so…

333
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:38,223
It's unavoidable that people think
I'm like him too.

334
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:39,433
No.

335
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:45,355
The sins of the father
are not the sins of the child.

336
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,441
Do you understand that?

337
00:17:56,992 --> 00:17:58,118
Miss Cita.

338
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:01,288
Is Karla here?

339
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:03,499
I just want to talk to her.

340
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:09,129
I'm sorry again about your wound.

341
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:12,966
No. It's fine.

342
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:15,511
It was my fault

343
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:17,805
for not introducing myself
to you right away.

344
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:19,098
[in English] Thank you.

345
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:20,974
[Uno sighs]

346
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:22,101
[Uno] I'll go home now.

347
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:27,439
Maybe tomorrow I'll figure out
how we can enter the secret room.

348
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:30,859
For sure, the laptop
I'm looking for is there.

349
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:34,113
Okay. I'll try to help you tomorrow.

350
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,406
- That's a promise, huh.
- Yes!

351
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:38,158
I'm sure.

352
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,701
[clicks tongue] Wait.

353
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:42,037
[light music playing]

354
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,373
[in English] Why are you touching Karla?

355
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:46,125
- Who are you?
- [chair scrapes]

356
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,460
[unsettling music playing]

357
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:51,380
Ah, he's Brother Atoy's colleague.

358
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,217
This is Gavin, my friend.

359
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:04,351
Uno, by the way.

360
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:07,271
- [in English] Future boyfriend of Karla.
- What?

361
00:19:08,063 --> 00:19:09,106
Really?

362
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:10,524
[in English] Manifesting.

363
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:19,449
[music fades]

364
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:23,871
You've slept here before, child,
so I'm sure you'll be comfortable.

365
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:27,249
The two of us fit perfectly here.

366
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,461
Janine.

367
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,629
[Janine sniffles]

368
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:34,756
Please talk to me.

369
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,596
Where's Daddy, Mommy?

370
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:45,142
I thought he was here?

371
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,978
And didn't you say

372
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,814
we were going to the US?

373
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:54,568
[pensive music playing]

374
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:04,453
Uncle Red and Aunt Martina,

375
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:07,623
why did they do that?

376
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,124
Why are they like that?

377
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:12,252
Why did they lock us up?

378
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:15,672
Mommy, I don't want to say this, but…

379
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,759
will they kill us?

380
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,428
What if…

381
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:25,432
What if they follow us here?

382
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:29,645
Daddy should be here

383
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:31,438
to protect us.

384
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:36,068
Janine, listen to me.

385
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:38,946
We're safe here.

386
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:43,200
But how can we be safe

387
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,828
if Daddy isn't here?

388
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,125
[tense music playing]

389
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:14,773
[melancholic music playing]

390
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:16,525
[dramatic sting]

391
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,865
[music fades]

392
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:27,869
[somber music playing]

393
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:58,233
Where are you, Atoy?

394
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:08,827
So much has happened here,
and still no word from you.

395
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:11,663
Your child and her mother are here.

396
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,833
They're waiting for you.

397
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:17,044
They need you.

398
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:20,130
Where are you?

399
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:23,633
[pensive music playing]

400
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:26,178
And…

401
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:31,558
You know I don't like it.
I'm the most handsome here.

402
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:33,977
So, what if…

403
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:36,855
What if I got burned in that fire?

404
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:40,650
Who would be the handsome one
left in our community?

405
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,488
That can't happen.

406
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:47,908
So please, Atoy.

407
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,494
Come back, please.

408
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:54,623
[mysterious voice] Psst.

409
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:55,540
‪[quirky sting]

410
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:59,252
[mysterious music playing]

411
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,308
Who's that?

412
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,269
Audrey?

413
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:18,230
Ame?

414
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:22,859
Janine?

415
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,154
[titters]

416
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:28,031
Don't scare me, okay?

417
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:29,366
You, huh.

418
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:31,618
You think I don't know it's you?

419
00:23:31,701 --> 00:23:33,328
[sneaky music playing]

420
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:35,831
[quirky sting]

421
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:38,500
Tonet?

422
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:42,295
Netchai, is that you?

423
00:23:44,422 --> 00:23:47,092
- [mysterious voice] Psst!
- [whimpers]

424
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:54,307
[playful music playing]

425
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:00,730
[mysterious voice] Psst!

426
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:01,648
[shrieks]

427
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:04,901
[music fades]

428
00:24:05,485 --> 00:24:07,320
[playful music playing]

429
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:11,700
[mysterious voice] Psst.

430
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,384
- [mysterious voice] Psst.
- [gasps]

431
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:31,803
Son of a thread.

432
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:45,108
[intense music playing]

433
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,362
Olga's child is dead.

434
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:52,365
I'm not fake. Why are you saying I'm fake?

435
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:55,535
Olga is a scammer.

436
00:24:55,619 --> 00:24:58,872
So, for sure, you're her fake child!

437
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:00,498
UP NEXT

438
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,543
[Emerson] A special personal mission
must be done

439
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:04,961
by the children of the thread.

440
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:10,050
We'll call this "Operation Atoy…

441
00:25:11,801 --> 00:25:12,636
Where are you?"

442
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,847
The ambassador's bodyguard.

443
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,599
His name is Samir.

444
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:19,684
I have a strong feeling

445
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:22,479
he's the reason why Atoy is missing.

446
00:25:23,063 --> 00:25:24,856
[grunting and groaning]

447
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:26,691
[groaning]

448
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:32,322
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

449
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,199
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

450
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:36,409
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
